    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim is partly upheld. The platform's GPS trace (EV-GPS-02808) measures the trip at 22.5 km against the booked optimal of 18.0 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02808) — an excess of 4.5 km, or 25.0%, which clears both POL-RD-01 gates (more than 20% of the optimal and more than 0.8 km). The trace is clean under POL-RD-07 (177 fixes at 10-second intervals, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s), so the deviation is established on the trace alone and no independent corroboration is needed. Your same-trip test under POL-RD-08(a) is also met: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry TRP-02808 and the trace window matches the trip's start and end.\n\nTo the driver: your traffic explanation is not made out under POL-RD-03. The LTA advisory (EV-ADVIS-02808-01) is genuine, is on file, names the PIE towards Tuas after Eunos Link, and its window (06:09:18–07:33:38) covers the trip, so limbs (a) and (b) are satisfied. Limb (c) is not. It requires an actual route that leaves the optimal corridor before the affected segment and rejoins it after, and the record does not show this: the trace never enters the advisory's area (0 fixes inside) and its closest approach to it is 1,203 m, so it never runs that corridor up to the affected segment and peels off. You carry the burden of the exculpatory clause (POL-RD-08) and it is not discharged. Your contemporaneous in-app message (EV-CHAT-02808, 06:40:48: 'accident on the PIE ahead, taking the alternative') is real evidence that you chose to divert, but POL-RD-13 tests a traffic assertion against the advisory, and the message does not supply the missing route shape. For completeness: had limb (c) been met, the cap (1.30 × (21.0 − 18.0) + 1.00 = 4.90 km) would have justified the whole 4.5 km and the closure-adjusted fare (29.875) would have exceeded the charge, giving no refund. Because it is not met, the excess stands at 4.5 km.\n\nThe refund is therefore arithmetic on the booked optimal route under POL-RD-02: recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 × 18.0 + 0.28 × 24.0) × 1.0) + 0.80 platform fee = 24.82; charged_total = 29.68; refund = 29.68 − 24.82 = 4.86, rounded up to SGD 4.90. The surge multiplier was read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier (EV-FARE-02808) and is 1.0.\n\nNothing else moves the numbers. POL-RD-09 adds nothing: there are no ERP lines and no airport surcharge (0.00). POL-RD-04 does not apply — the only chat message is from the driver, is not a rider instruction, and carries waypoint_hint null. POL-RD-05 does not apply (no amendment; amended_optimal_distance_km is null) and POL-RD-12 does not apply (vehicle_type RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL), so the 18.0 km booked optimal is the correct baseline. No repeat-deviation pattern is established — deviation_flags_90d is 0 and 0 of 399 completed trips is 0.0, below the POL-RD-06 thresholds — so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct referral; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and cannot be substituted. The rider's profile does not trigger any extra corroboration requirement (deviation_claims_60d is 1, below the POL-RD-08 threshold of 4).\n\nThe refund of SGD 4.90 is 16.4% of the charge: above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% full-refund share, so this is a partial refund. It does not exceed the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold and will execute on issue. Confidence is 0.85; every artifact carrying a deciding fact is at weight 1.0."
